{{- /*
What enrolling a tree writes for Codex: the PreToolUse hook that routes a
command through the broker, merged into the tree's own .codex/hooks.json, which
Codex reads alongside the account-wide one.

Both files load and both hooks run, the account's first. That costs a second
pass over the deny list on every call and nothing else: what the account's hook
refuses, this one refuses too, and only this one rewrites.

It goes in git's ignores rather than the repository, everything here naming a
path this machine decided.

The matcher is "*" for the reason the account-wide one is: an empty reply is a
call left alone, and matching every tool is what puts apply_patch in front of
the deny list.

Codex does not run a hook it has not been told to trust, and says nothing when
it skips one. See the note `faramir init-project` prints.
*/ -}}
{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": {{ quote (printf "%s/faramir guard --host codex" .BinDir) }},
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
